<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">Generalizable Geometric Prior and Recurrent Spiking Feature Learning for Humanoid Robot Manipulation<span class="ltx_pubnotes"><span class="ltx_pubnotes_content"><span class="ltx_pubnote ltx_role_thanks"><span class="ltx_note_name">Thanks: </span>
The authors are with the School of Computer Science, School of Robotics, Institute of Technological Sciences, Wuhan University, Wuhan, China 430072. E-mail:{xtli312, wenkehuang, yemang, jxuan, dubo, shengliu, miao.li}@whu.edu.cn, (Xuetao Li and Wenke Huang contributed equally, Jifeng Xuan and Miao Li are corresponding authors).
A preliminary version of this work has appeared in Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI 2026) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite>.
</span></span></span></h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Xuetao Li<a href="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4206-7612" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">
